# Always commit & push

When a coherent chunk of work is done (feature, fix, docs/rules, e2e, etc.):

1. **Commit** with a concise message (follow existing git commit style / HEREDOC).
2. **Push** to `origin` immediately (`git push -u origin HEAD` when needed).
3. **Do not ask** “want me to commit/push?” — just do it.

Still follow git safety: no force-push to main/master, no config changes, no skipping hooks, no committing secrets. If there is nothing to commit, skip silently.
